## Corrected lane L1: Pill refactor and `usePermalink` hook

The earlier attempt probably failed the `@room` test because `usePermalink` resolved everything inside a `useEffect`, so the first render returned nothing and the pill appeared only after an effect. This version resolves type, text, avatar and resource ID synchronously during render. The only async work is the profile lookup for user pills that have no local member.

Two other changes:
- `usePermalink` no longer builds its sigil-to-type table at module load. `Pill.tsx` and `usePermalink.tsx` import each other, so a top-level `PillType.X` reference could hit an undefined enum.
- The leftover `_PillTypeExport` and `_unusedPillMarker` debris is removed.

I have not run the tests.

